ext: the White House Correspondents' Dinner was rescheduled after an earlier postponement. On July 25, 2026, during his speech, President Trump mocked CNN's Kaitlan Collins, calling her award \"fake\" and telling her to \"smile more.\" He then compared Collins to Dylan Mulvaney, referencing Mulvaney Bud Light partnership and calling it the \"worst commercial ever made.\" The story took a darker turn when, on July 27, 2026, Mulvaney posted a TikTok responding to Trump remarks. Mulvaney stated she viewed his criticism as a compliment and emphasized the importance of acknowledging authentic selves to support trans and nonbinary individuals. Reportedly, Trump later doubled down on his comments, posting an AI-generated image. The full dated timeline is on GenZHype dot com.","image":"https://genzhype.com/assets/covers/dylan-mulvaney-responds-to-donald-trump-s-white-house-correspondents-dinner-remarks-vs.webp","visuals":["https://genzhype.com/assets/covers/dylan-mulvaney-responds-to-donald-trump-s-white-house-correspondents-dinner-remarks-vs.webp","https://variety.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/dylan-trump.jpg?w=1000&h=563&crop=1","https://d1rldr9jdodfaa.cloudfront.net/images/01KYHDWM1Y0PHZ592X4M2649PC/8d524e8d-f999-4bfa-b469-ff9edf6f4de0_1785143906.webp","https://media.radaronline.com/brand-img/7rc8_M1uH/1200x628/kaitlan-collins-clap-back-donald-trump-compared-dylan-mulvaney-5-1785081176109.jpg","https://i.ytimg.com/vi/lezRuElACEQ/maxresdefault.jpg","https://i.ytimg.com/vi/Aw_-TzZCmKQ/maxresdefault.jpg","https://i.ytimg.com/vi/JnczIFGBShM/maxresdefault.jpg"],"visual_titles":["cover photo of the story","the actual moment (Nov 30 report photo): Original White House Correspondents' Dinner Postponed","the actual moment (Jul 25 report photo): Rescheduled White House Correspondents' Dinner Held","the actual moment (Jul 27 report photo): Mulvaney Reposts Eleanor Roosevelt Quote","recent photo of Dylan Mulvaney (their May video)","recent photo of Dylan Mulvaney (their May video)"